{
 "schema": "br-qctx4/br-g11iy readfix A/B v1",
 "rule": "Read-path fixes A/B (br-qctx4 + fetch_inbox no-op receipt write). Written 2026-10-14 ~03:35Z, before the variant\nbuild finished and before any run of this experiment.\n\nChange under test (readfix_v1.patch, sha256 0f9df67c...):\n  1. br-qctx4: fetch_inbox's direct read = three single-table statements (recipient rows by agent index, messages by PK\n     in chunks, senders by id) instead of a recipients JOIN messages that FrankenSQLite plans as a full recipients scan.\n  2. fetch_inbox no longer asks for read receipts on rows that already carry one, and the sync batch recounts\n     inbox_stats only when a receipt flipped. Before: every non-empty mark_read fetch opened a fresh connection, took\n     BEGIN IMMEDIATE, ran a no-op UPDATE, DELETE + full recount + INSERT of inbox_stats, and committed.\n\nArms (same commit, same flags, run_release_build4.sh, portable features; worker noted per arm):\n  A = build31/v039 (a4ec56bc, shipped v0.3.39 source; built on vmi1149989)\n  B = build33/readfix_v1b (a4ec56bc + readfix_v1.patch; built on vmi1227854/hz3/vmi1152480 after vmi1149989 refused under critical disk pressure; no target-cpu flags, same pinned toolchain)\n\nHarness: mixed_rate.py, 2 senders A->B paced at 4 sends/s total (open loop), 2 closed-loop readers fetch_inbox(B,\nlimit 20), 1 search loop, 1 Hz health, 300 s. Two modes, each run A B B A under the host lock, nothing else of mine on\nthe host (the NAS relocation must have finished):\n  Mode R: readers mark_read=true (the tool default; what agents actually call).\n  Mode P: readers mark_read=false (peek; the soak's shape). Here change 2 cannot act, and recipients == B's inbox, so\n          change 1 has no O(table) work to remove: Mode P is the regression guard for the three-statement read.\n\nValidity per run: >= 1,140 of 1,200 scheduled sends succeed; read error rate <= 1%. An invalid run is rerun once, then\nthe arm is reported as failing.\n\nDecision:\n  Mode P guard: pooled B read count >= 0.90 x A AND pooled B read p50 <= 1.15 x A. Failing it means the three-statement\n    read is slower where the inbox is the whole table: change 1 does not land as is (the recount_scaling/direct2 benches\n    pick the alternative shape), whatever Mode R says.\n  Mode R WIN: pooled B read count >= 1.15 x A AND pooled B send p99 <= 1.10 x A. Report as a self-speedup\n    (MAINTENANCE), not a campaign win.\n  Mode R NULL: neither WIN nor regression (B reads >= 0.95 x A and send p99 <= 1.10 x A): change 2 lands as hygiene with\n    the measured null stated and no speed claim.\n  Mode R REGRESSION: B reads < 0.95 x A or send p99 > 1.10 x A: change 2 is reverted.\nReported, not deciding: per-window read p50 vs sends_before for both arms; send p50; search counts.\n\nAMENDMENT 2026-10-14 ~05:20Z, before any run of this experiment (readfix_ab/ does not exist; the runner was stopped\nwhile still waiting): the variant is rebuilt as B = build33/readfix_v2 (a4ec56bc + readfix_v2.patch). v2 = v1 plus\nbr-qctx4 step 2 reading `messages` by rowid seek (the IN query no longer carries ORDER BY/LIMIT, which made\nFrankenSQLite 0.4.10 scan and sort the whole table; per the planner source read). That is what lands, so it is what is\nmeasured. Decision thresholds, harness, modes and order are unchanged. Built incrementally in rc1013d on\nvmi1152480/vmi1227854/hz3 after readfix_v1b; v1b is not run.\n  readfix_v2.patch sha256 73ab1adb67b2c358... (git diff of rc1013d at a4ec56bc: sync.rs, query_plan_diagnostics.rs, messaging.rs); build started 2026-10-14T05:35:15Z.\n",
